# The GNSS HAL cannot reach the framework sensor service.
#
#   avc: denied { find } for pid=1913 uid=1021
#     name=android.frameworks.sensorservice.ISensorManager/default
#     scontext=u:r:vendor_hal_gnss_qti:s0
#     tcontext=u:object_r:fwk_sensor_service:s0 tclass=service_manager permissive=0
#
# The consumer is libsensorndkbridge.so, which the QTI GNSS HAL uses for
# sensor-assisted positioning -- SAP / motion aiding, i.e. dead reckoning and
# stationary detection between fixes.
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS NOT WHY A FIX TAKES TIME, AND IT IS NOT WHY GPS LOOKED BROKEN.
# GPS works: measured outdoors, timeUncertaintyNs 6.0e9 -> 149 (the engine
# demodulated GNSS time directly, which NTP injection at +/-15ms cannot produce)
# and horizontalAccuracyMeters 155446 -> 21.2. Acquisition needs sky view, not
# this rule. Ship it because stock grants it and we should not diverge, not
# because it fixes a symptom.
#
# Stock's counterpart, verbatim from its precompiled policy
# (/vendor/etc/selinux/vendor_sepolicy.cil):
#   (allow vendor_hal_gnss_qti fwk_sensor_service_34_0 (service_manager (find)))
# fwk_sensor_service_34_0 is the versioned mapping type; the unversioned
# fwk_sensor_service is what our denial names and what this tree has.
#
# Note rild takes the same denial against the same service. Left alone here:
# nothing has been shown to depend on it, and this file is about GNSS.
allow vendor_hal_gnss_qti fwk_sensor_service:service_manager find;
